id: pm-review-github-d686d81c4a08-14
title: Exact-head completion accepts unavailable-review notices and rejects substantive rate-limit reviews
description: "GH issue #14: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/issues/14 · author @unbraind · created 2026-10-16T10:01:49Z · updated 2026-10-16T23:34:31Z"
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-review#14","github_author:unbraind"
created_at: "2026-10-17T05:38:36.259Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T22:35:36.071Z"
author: pm-github
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T22:35:36.062Z",codex-agent,"PR #27 extends this issue regression protection to the new criterion coverage path. Substantive attributed allowance/quota/rate-limit counter findings remain eligible through real SDK and registered review cover; genuine quota-exhausted/skipped/unavailable/rate-limit-reached notices remain refused. The topic-wide denylist was narrowed to service-notice phrases, with an isolated revert proof. Work and verification are tracked on pm-review-criterion-coverage-map. This does not change or certify the existing round-completion classifier; this issue remains open."
body: "## Summary\n\nThe exact-head CodeRabbit completion predicate uses a separate raw substring denylist instead of the actionable-aware notice classification used elsewhere. As a result, it accepts some unavailable-review notices as completed reviews and rejects substantive reviews that discuss rate-limit handling.\n\nReproduced at **58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50**, package/manifest version **2026.10.12** (README still explicitly unreleased), with Node **v24.19.0** on Linux x86_64. The source-dispatch integration also used the retained official **@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.13**, matching this source's exact devDependency and minimum host. This is source acceptance, not a published npm/Bun artifact or deployed-host claim.\n\n## Expected and actual\n\nBoth cases below are submitted `COMMENTED` reviews by `coderabbitai[bot]` on the exact current head, with successful checks, no unresolved threads, the required author vote, and retained imported context.\n\n| Review body | Package notice classifier | Expected completion evidence | Actual completion evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `Quota exhausted` | `isReviewNotice=true` | false | true |\n| `**High**\\nAdd retry backoff for rate-limit responses before writes.` | `isReviewNotice=false`; actionable import | true | false |\n\nThe second case has a recorded final fix and fixing SHA. All status blocker lists are empty; only the completion predicate keeps the gate false.\n\nThe complete 12-case independent oracle also finds false positives for `No access to this repository`, `Action not completed`, `Failed to generate review`, and `This repository does not receive automatic reviews.` Controls `Review failed`, `Rate-limit exceeded`, `Review skipped`, and `Trial ended` remain incomplete, while an empty submitted review and `No actionable issues.` remain eligible.\n\n## Minimal offline reproduction\n\nIn a checkout of the exact commit, save this as `repro.mjs` and run `node repro.mjs`. It uses source modules only, requires no provider credentials, and performs no network or tracker writes.\n\n```js\nimport { evaluateRound } from './src/round.ts';\nimport { findingsOf, isReviewNotice } from './src/findings.ts';\nconst head = 'a'.repeat(40);\nfor (const body of ['Quota exhausted', '**High**\\nAdd retry backoff for rate-limit responses before writes.']) {\n  const pr = {\n    repo: 'example/package', number: 1, head, headDate: '2026-10-16T07:00:00Z', author: 'author',\n    threads: [], comments: [], commits: [], checks: [{ name: 'CI', state: 'pass' }],\n    reviews: [{ id: 'review-1', bot: 'coderabbitai[bot]', isBot: true, body,\n      url: 'https://github.com/example/package/pull/1#pullrequestreview-1',\n      createdAt: '2026-10-16T08:00:00Z', head, state: 'COMMENTED',\n      reactions: [{ content: 'THUMBS_UP', user: 'author' }] }],\n  };\n  const items = findingsOf(pr).map(f => ({\n    id: 'tracked-review', type: 'ReviewFinding', status: 'closed',\n    review_repo: pr.repo, review_pr: pr.number, review_node_id: f.id,\n    review_verdict: f.verdict === 'informational' ? 'informational' : 'fix',\n  }));\n  const result = evaluateRound(pr, items);\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({ body, notice: isReviewNotice(body),\n    coderabbit_finished: result.coderabbit_finished, complete: result.complete }));\n}\n```\n\nObserved:\n\n```json\n{\"body\":\"Quota exhausted\",\"notice\":true,\"coderabbit_finished\":true,\"complete\":true}\n{\"body\":\"**High**\\nAdd retry backoff for rate-limit responses before writes.\",\"notice\":false,\"coderabbit_finished\":false,\"complete\":false}\n```\n\n## Integration and preservation evidence\n\nAn independent real-filesystem SDK fixture imported the quota review as `informational` and `closed`. The unmodified `runReviewCommand` dispatcher, exercised through `activateExtensionForTest` / `runRegisteredCommandForTest` with only the transport boundary injected, returned for `review status`:\n\n```json\n{\"handled\":true,\"result\":{\"complete\":true,\"unvoted_bot_items\":[],\"findings_without_verdict\":[],\"verdicts_without_reply\":[],\"stale_replies\":[],\"unresolved_threads\":[],\"current_head_review_completed\":true},\"warnings\":[]}\n```\n\nAfter changing the same source to the substantive review body, import correctly reopened it as pending. A recorded fix with SHA then left all blocker lists empty, but status returned `complete=false`, `current_head_review_completed=false`, and host `exitCode=1`. Transport calls were synthetic; no GitHub reads/writes or paid calls were made by this execution.\n\nAll **77** focused authored tests from `core.test.ts`, `github.test.ts`, `review-regressions.test.ts` and `respond.test.ts` passed without skips. Independent replay preserved imported identity, local verdict/reason/commit and the single audit comment; reconcile dry-run and failed-read controls made no durable changes; applied reconciliation retained prior history bytes; retry added no closure history; 21 repeated read-only query probes left durable tracker/schema/history bytes unchanged. All six fixture history streams pass verification and both structural validations return ok=true; the active notice fixture reports missing acceptance-criteria/estimate metadata warnings, while the main fixture is warning-free. These controls do not eliminate the uncovered completion mismatch above.\n\n## Cause and owner lineage\n\n- [Completion predicate](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50/src/round.ts#L17-L20) only rejects `review failed|rate[- ]limit|review skipped|trial (?:has )?ended` anywhere in the review body\n- [Existing actionable-aware notice predicate](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50/src/findings.ts#L15-L18) recognizes the broader notice family and retains substantive findings\n- [Canonical round owner](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50/.agents/pm/features/pm-review-round.toon), delivered by #1\n- [Related provider-notice classification item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50/.agents/pm/issues/pm-review-pr7r.toon), delivered by #1\n- [Status integration owner](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50/.agents/pm/features/pm-review-respond.toon), delivered by #12\n\nThis is distinct from the already-open [round success exit-code contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/blob/58ea2c294137f4e392931dad8bb0af4d054bbc50/.agents/pm/issues/pm-review-round-exit-contract.toon), also reproduced during this review: the successful round source result emits explicit zero, rejected by host normalization. Status omits explicit zero, so the false-green status above survives real host normalization. No duplicate exit-contract issue is requested.\n\nAll-status issues/PRs and relevant #1/#8/#9/#12 discussions were checked for this classification mismatch before filing. No equivalent open or closed finding was found.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. All explicitly unavailable/incomplete notice bodies above fail completed-review evidence through both round and status, even when submitted for the exact head and every other condition is satisfied\n2. A substantive severity-marked review about rate-limit handling remains eligible after its findings have been decided; quoted notice words cannot incorrectly erase substantive review evidence\n3. Cover both cases through the source evaluator and actual registered-host dispatch with real temporary trackers, not only raw handler return assertions\n4. Preserve exact-head, review state/author, complete pagination, live thread/vote, import completeness, durable verdict/history and no-write-on-failure contracts; empty submitted review and genuine no-actionable-review controls remain supported\n5. Keep source and shipped-artifact validation separate; run packed consumers when the authorized toolchain is available\n\nNo implementation, source pin, original tracker, remote review state, merge or release was changed by this review.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-16T23:34:31Z)\n>\n> Retested on current main [51cd1993858e9af5d35b1d846c86267da406e9f7](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/tree/51cd1993858e9af5d35b1d846c86267da406e9f7), after merged #16, using Node v24.19.0 and the unchanged pinned @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.13.\n> \n> The existing classification defect remains, with one important reachability change: #16 correctly removes the unrelated successful-round exit-code failure, so the unavailable-review false green now survives host normalization through **both `review round` and `review status`**.\n> \n> - Exact-head submitted `COMMENTED` review containing only `Quota exhausted`: import records informational/closed; both registered-host commands return `handled: true`, `complete: true`, no failure exit code, and empty blocker lists\n> - Exact-head substantive review `**High**\\nAdd retry backoff for rate-limit responses before writes.`, after a recorded fix with SHA: both commands remain incomplete with host exitCode 1 solely because completed-review evidence is false; all other blocker lists are empty\n> \n> Both cases use real isolated filesystem trackers and the unmodified current source dispatcher through the SDK registered-host normalization path, with a synthetic injected provider boundary. No live review operation was performed.\n> \n> Current focused authored suite: **78 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** across core, GitHub transport, review regressions and respond tests. This includes #16's six schema-type declarations and numeric/boolean persisted round trips. A separate 12-scenario replay using unchanged registered handlers, real transport code and synthetic fetch responses passes complete/incomplete/refusal cases for round JSON, compact, compact+JSON and status JSON. The existing 12-case classifier oracle still has the same six mismatches. Independent import/verdict/reconciliation/history-preservation checks also pass.\n> \n> This is additional evidence for #14, not a new defect or a regression in #16's exit-code fix. Source/registered-host validation only; no packed npm/Bun acceptance, full release gate or deployed-host claim."
